        "Content": "***SUBSTANTIAL 3-BEDROOM SEMI-DETACHED HOME / B RATED / FULLY INSULATED / BRAND NEW BOILER & HEATING SYSTEM / FLOORED ATTIC STORAGE / GARAGE / LARGE FRONT & REAR GARDENS / GENEROUS ROOM PROPORTIONS / TWO BATHROOMS / ESTABLISHED FAMILY LOCATION / EXCELLENT POTENTIAL***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW are delighted to introduce No. 86 Glasnevin Avenue, Dublin 11 to the market.\r\n\r\nThere is something particularly appealing about a home that gives you space to make it your own and 86 Glasnevin Avenue is a lovely example of just that, a substantial three-bedroom semi-detached house, set on a generous site with gardens to both front and rear, a garage and wonderfully well-proportioned accommodation throughout.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 110 sq. m., the house has all the ingredients of a very comfortable family home as it stands, while also offering plenty of opportunity for its next owners to modernise and, subject to planning permission, perhaps take it further over time.\r\n\r\nAn added benefit of No. 86 is the significant investment that has already been made in the home's energy efficiency and heating. The property has been fully insulated, while the boiler, heating system and associated piping have all been replaced, providing a modern and efficient system for the new owners. The attic has also been partially floored, providing excellent additional storage, a particularly useful feature for a family home of this size.\r\n\r\nFrom the moment you arrive, there is a lovely sense of space. The front garden is generous and mature, with established planting and a low brick wall, while the driveway provides off-street parking and leads to the garage. The traditional red-brick and pebbledash exterior gives the house a warm, established feel that sits beautifully within this mature Glasnevin setting.\r\n\r\nInside, the proportions are immediately apparent. The entrance hall is bright and welcoming, with the principal living spaces arranged naturally off it and the staircase rising to the first floor.\r\n\r\nThe living room is positioned to the front of the house and is a wonderfully generous reception room. A large picture window fills the room with natural light and looks out over the front garden, while the fireplace provides a natural focal point. There is plenty of room here for comfortable family living, with the kind of proportions that are becoming harder to find in more recently built homes.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the kitchen is very much the heart of the house. It is a large, practical space with a good amount of fitted storage and worktop space, as well as plenty of room for a family dining table. Large windows overlook the rear garden, bringing in lovely natural light and creating a pleasant connection with the garden beyond. \r\n\r\nThere is also a wonderful sense of possibility here. The kitchen works perfectly well as it is, but for someone looking to put their own stamp on the property, it offers a fantastic starting point for a more contemporary kitchen and dining space.\r\n\r\nAdjoining the kitchen is a further reception room which is particularly versatile. It could be used as a family room, playroom, home office or simply as a second sitting room, a really useful space for a growing family and one that can adapt as life changes.\r\n\r\nThe rear garden is another of the home's real highlights. Exceptionally generous in size and well established, it is framed by beautiful mature planting and hedging, with a good-sized lawn and plenty of room for children to play, summer dining or simply enjoying the garden. It has a lovely sense of privacy and greenery, and is a particularly pleasant outlook from the rear of the house.\r\n\r\nA guest WC completes the ground floor, while the garage provides excellent additional storage and practical space. It also offers the potential to be incorporated into a future project, subject to the necessary permissions.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, with the principal bedroom being particularly generous. The second bedroom is also a very good double room, while the third is an ideal child's bedroom, guest room or home office. The family bathroom completes the accommodation upstairs.\r\n\r\nWhat I particularly like about No. 86 is the combination of space, garden and potential. This is not a house where everything has simply been done to someone else's taste, and that is part of its appeal. There is already a substantial and very comfortable home here, with generous rooms, good natural light and lovely gardens. For those who want to modernise and create something more personal, there is also plenty to work with. Importantly, some of the significant practical improvements have already been taken care of, including the insulation, new boiler and upgraded heating system. It is a house that can grow with its owners, and one where the possibilities will become apparent as soon as you walk through the door.\r\n\r\nNow a little on the location! Glasnevin Avenue is situated within a long-established residential part of Dublin 11, surrounded by mature homes, established gardens and a wonderful selection of amenities.\r\n\r\nIt is an especially popular location with families, with a choice of well-regarded schools within easy reach, including Glasnevin Educate Together, Glasnevin National School, St. Brigid's Girls National School, Scoil Mobhi and Gaelscoil Áine. There are also a number of secondary schools in the surrounding area, including St. Mary's Holy Faith Secondary School, St. Vincent's CBS and Trinity Comprehensive. For those with children attending third level, DCU is also within easy reach, while the National Botanic Gardens is close by and provides one of the area's most beautiful and much-loved amenities.\r\n\r\nThere is plenty here for everyday life too. Albert College Park, Griffith Park and the Tolka Valley are all within the wider area and offer wonderful spaces for walking, running and enjoying the outdoors. Glasnevin Village has a lovely community feel, with local shops, cafés and services, while neighbouring Drumcondra and Phibsborough add an even greater choice of restaurants, coffee shops and independent businesses.\r\n\r\nFor commuters, the location is exceptionally convenient, with regular bus services serving the area and easy access to the city centre, M50 and Dublin Airport.\r\n\r\nAnd perhaps this is what makes Glasnevin so appealing, you have the feeling of an established residential neighbourhood, with mature trees, gardens and familiar streetscapes, while still being just a short distance from the energy and amenities of Dublin city.\r\n\r\nNo. 86 Glasnevin Avenue is a home with great bones, generous proportions and an excellent sense of space. The gardens, garage and substantial accommodation are all wonderful assets, while the recent investment in insulation, heating and the new boiler means some of the important practical upgrades have already been taken care of. There is still plenty of scope to modernise and make the house your own, making this a particularly exciting opportunity. For anyone looking for a genuine family home in a well-established Glasnevin location, this is a property well worth seeing.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
